<%# Reference chip (Bezugs-Sammlung S2, §8.1). Same shape as the scope chip
    beside it -- a small faint label, then the value -- because the two answer
    neighbouring questions ("what is this about", "where do we look") and two
    different shapes would read as two unrelated controls. `contents` puts it into
    the shared row (see ChatContainerComponent's template).

    Always the SET state: the chip does not exist without a reference, so there is
    no empty pill and no placeholder.

    THREE states, and only the WRAPPER tells them apart: nothing (render? is
    false), one pill, and from two entries on a <details> whose summary counts
    them by type. The entries themselves are captured ONCE below -- a pill for one
    and a differently built row for many would be two shapes to keep in step,
    while they carry the same three things either way (icon, capped title, own
    remove address). The collapsing pattern is not new: citation_list_component
    does exactly this with <details>/<summary> and no JavaScript. %>
<%# data-reference-keys: the chip says WHICH objects it stands for, so the panel
    can tell the offer of step 5b apart from a reference that already points at
    the page you are on. The panel reads the DOM here because it is the only
    channel it has: its own node is permanent, the server never re-renders it,
    and the chip is what the server said LAST. A second copy of the keys on the
    permanent node would be a copy that drifts.

    On the OUTER element, and it stays there in both states: it is the turbo
    anchor and the panel's channel, and neither may depend on how many entries
    there happen to be. %>
<% entries = capture do %>
  <% references.each do |record| %>
    <% title = title_for(record) %>
    <%# The pill carries the value AND the remove button, so the two read as one
        object rather than as a label with a stray x next to it. max-w + truncate
        for the 380px panel: the title is free text and the row must not push the
        style pills off the line -- and inside the open list the same cap keeps a
        pasted stacktrace from turning one entry into three lines. %>
    <%# div and not span: the pill contains a form (the remove button), and a form
        inside phrasing content is invalid nesting. %>
    <div class="inline-flex max-w-[13rem] items-center gap-1 rounded-full border border-ink bg-cream-200 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-cream-900">
      <%# The type's own glyph, from the citation map (see #icon_for). Decorative:
          the title beside it already says what this is, and from S3 on the KIND is
          what tells two entries of one collection apart at a glance. %>
      <i class="bi <%= icon_for(record) %> shrink-0 text-[10px] text-cream-700" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span class="truncate" title="<%= title %>"><%= title %></span>
      <%# The only write this chip has: taking ONE entry back out, by a DELETE on
          that entry's own address (§7.1). Removal now NAMES what it removes
          instead of clearing a column. `contents` again, so the button sits
          inside the pill instead of below it. Same turbo_frame as the scope
          chip's form -- both answer with the same stream, which replaces the
          whole row.

          Nothing here touches the scope chip, and since E3 nothing anywhere
          does: the reference names the SUBJECT, the chip is the user's own
          narrowing, and only the user writes it. The old chip asked for both
          columns through two hidden fields, back when removing the last
          reference also cleared the project. %>
      <%= form_with url: remove_url(record), method: :delete,
                    data: { turbo_frame: 'assistant_panel_body' },
                    class: 'contents' do %>
        <%# focus-visible ring like the house contract (Neo::Buttons::Base): this is
            the only destructive control in the row, and `focus:outline-none` alone
            was pure removal -- the select's reason for it does not carry over,
            @tailwindcss/forms rings form fields, not buttons. Without ring-offset:
            the button sits INSIDE a filled pill, and the offset would paint a
            white halo on the cream fill.

            w-6 h-6: a 10px glyph with 4px of side padding was an 18x10 target,
            the same shape the offer strip's dismiss button grew a 24x24 hit box
            for. The negative vertical margin keeps the pill at its height. %>
        <button type="submit"
                class="-my-1 -mr-1 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-cream-700 transition-colors hover:text-cream-900 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ink"
                aria-label="<%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.reference.remove', title: title) %>">
          <i class="bi bi-x-lg text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
<div id="<%= dom_id %>" class="contents" data-reference-keys="<%= reference_keys %>">
  <% if collection? %>
    <%# ⚠️ open:basis-full, and it has to sit on the element that carries the
        `open` attribute: the Tailwind variant is `&[open]`, so it reaches no
        ancestor. Without it the open list does not break out of the context row,
        it grows INSIDE it -- and the scope chip, vertically centred beside it,
        ends up wedged between the label and the list. With it the whole block
        takes its own line of the wrapping row and "Sucht in" drops below it,
        which is where the layout spec measures it.

        min-w-0 so the summary's truncation has something to truncate against;
        `group` for the chevron below. %>
    <details class="group min-w-0 open:basis-full" <%= tag.attributes(open: expanded?) %>>
      <%# list-none: the native marker is a triangle at the start of the line,
          which would sit to the LEFT of the "Bezug" label and read as a bullet.
          The chevron below says the same thing at the end, where the eye is after
          reading the count. cursor-pointer because a summary is a control that
          does not otherwise look like one. %>
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none select-none items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-xs text-faint"><%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.reference.label') %></span>
        <span class="inline-flex max-w-[13rem] items-center gap-1 rounded-full border border-ink bg-cream-200 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-cream-900">
          <span class="truncate"><%= summary_label %></span>
          <i class="bi bi-chevron-down shrink-0 text-[10px] transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <%# One line per object (§8.1), not a wrapped band of pills: at ten entries a
          wrapped band is a block whose height nobody can predict, and an eye
          looking for the one to remove has no column to run down. mt-1.5 lines up
          with the row's own gap-y. %>
      <div class="mt-1.5 flex flex-col items-start gap-1">
        <%= entries %>
      </div>
    </details>
  <% else %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
      <span class="text-xs text-faint"><%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.reference.label') %></span>
      <%= entries %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
